  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: ClinComm 2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "Researchers notice low trial enrollment from certain neighborhoods.
    They reach out to your local advocacy group for guidance. \r\n\r\nCommunity advocates
    can help identify barriers to participation and suggest ways to reach more diverse
    communities. \r\nIs this true or false?\r\n"
  explanation: Community advocates understand the challenges that may prevent people
    from joining clinical trials, such as transportation, time, or language barriers.
    By sharing this insight, they help researchers think about more inclusive recruitment
    strategies. This encourages participation from diverse communities. In turn,
    it helps ensure trial results better reflect real-world patients.
  correctAnswer: True
  incorrectAnswer1: False
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Community Advocate
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Clinical
